    title: "What is the Repository pattern and why use it over direct CRUD functions?",
    summary: "The Repository pattern wraps data access behind an abstraction with a defined interface, decoupling business logic from the specific persistence technology.",
    explanation: "Where simple CRUD functions are tightly coupled to SQLAlchemy, a repository defines an interface (often an abstract base class or Protocol) like UserRepository with methods such as get_by_id and save, and a concrete implementation like SqlAlchemyUserRepository fulfills it. This makes it straightforward to swap implementations (e.g., for testing, use an in-memory repository) or migrate persistence layers without rewriting business logic, at the cost of extra boilerplate that may be overkill for small CRUD-only services.",
